{
  "id": "ee1-13",
  "number": 13,
  "title": "Logic II: 555 clock, decade counter and 7-segment display",
  "topics": ["Logic circuits", "Discrete circuits", "Test and measurement instruments"],
  "goal": "Make a clock with a 555 timer, count its pulses with a 7490 decade counter and show the count on a 7-segment display through a 7447 decoder.",
  "theory": [
    "In astable mode a 555 charges its capacitor through R_A + R_B and discharges it through R_B, so it runs at f = 1.44/((R_A + 2R_B)·C) with a HIGH time 0.693·(R_A + R_B)·C and a LOW time 0.693·R_B·C.",
    "A 7490 holds a divide-by-2 (input CKA, output QA) and a divide-by-5 (CKB → QB, QC, QD). Wiring QA to CKB makes a BCD counter 0–9: QA toggles at f/2 and QD completes one cycle every ten clocks (f/10). It counts on falling edges.",
    "A 7447 turns the 4-bit BCD code DCBA into the seven segment drives a–g. Its outputs are active-LOW and open-collector, made for a common-anode display: COM to +5 V and each segment through about 330 Ω to the decoder.",
    "On a scope, trigger on the clock and compare QA and QD with it; a logic probe blinks on every change."
  ],
  "prelab": [
    { "key": "f", "label": "555 frequency, R_A = 10 kΩ, R_B = 47 kΩ, C = 4.7 µF", "unit": "Hz", "answer": "1.44/((10000+2*47000)*4.7e-6)" },
    { "key": "duty", "label": "Clock duty cycle (HIGH time / period)", "unit": "%", "answer": "100*(10000+47000)/(10000+2*47000)" },
    { "key": "fqa", "label": "QA frequency", "unit": "Hz", "answer": "1.44/((10000+2*47000)*4.7e-6)/2" },
    { "key": "fqd", "label": "QD frequency", "unit": "Hz", "answer": "1.44/((10000+2*47000)*4.7e-6)/10" }
  ],
  "procedure": [
    "Load the reference build. The display counts 0, 1, 2 … 9 and starts again — about three counts a second.",
    "Scope CH1 on the 555 output (column 7), CH2 on QA (column 22). Read both frequencies and the clock's duty cycle with the cursors.",
    "Turn RUN off (logic switch on the 555's RESET pin): the clock stops and the count freezes.",
    "Try C = 0.47 µF: the count becomes a blur, but the scope still measures f ten times higher.",
    "Optional: use the DAQ's DIO lines or the logic probe to read QA–QD while the clock runs slowly."
  ],
  "table": [
    { "key": "fm", "label": "Clock frequency (CH1)", "unit": "Hz", "predict": "f", "source": "scope.ch1.freq", "tol": 10 },
    { "key": "fqam", "label": "QA frequency (CH2)", "unit": "Hz", "predict": "fqa", "source": "scope.ch2.freq", "tol": 10 }
  ],
  "checks": [
    { "kind": "freq", "label": "555 runs at 1.44/((R_A + 2R_B)·C)", "ref": "j7", "window": 2.5, "expect": "1.44/((RA+2*RB)*CT)", "tol": 0.1 },
    { "kind": "freq", "label": "QA divides the clock by two", "ref": "d22", "window": 3, "expect": "1.44/((RA+2*RB)*CT)/2", "tol": 0.12 },
    { "kind": "segments", "label": "Display reads 0 with the clock held in reset", "set": [{ "part": "RUN", "key": "on", "value": false }], "part": "DS1", "lit": "abcdef" }
  ],
  "settle": 0.4,
  "build": {
    "version": 1,
    "name": "EE Lab I · 13 Counter",
    "components": [
      { "id": "PS", "type": "bench_supply", "pos": { "x": -18.5, "z": 20 }, "params": { "v1": 12, "v2": 12, "i1": 0.2, "i2": 0.2 } },
      { "id": "SC", "type": "oscilloscope", "pos": { "x": 2, "z": 21 } },
      { "id": "U1", "type": "ne555", "at": "f5" },
      { "id": "RA", "type": "resistor", "params": { "resistance": 10000 }, "holes": ["a6", "top+7"] },
      { "id": "RB", "type": "resistor", "params": { "resistance": 47000 }, "holes": ["b6", "b7"] },
      { "id": "CT", "type": "capacitor", "params": { "capacitance": 4.7e-6 }, "holes": ["h6", "bot-6"] },
      { "id": "RUN", "type": "logic_switch", "params": { "on": true }, "holes": ["bot+9", "j8", "bot-10"] },
      { "id": "U2", "type": "sn7490", "at": "f20" },
      { "id": "U3", "type": "sn7447", "at": "f40" },
      { "id": "DS1", "type": "seven_segment_ca", "at": "f53" },
